WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:03.230
Japan’s #1 bakery chain, Pantasia,

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:07.570
was to gather the newcomers from all 128
of its branches from the country at once

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:12.990
to hold a serious newcomers battle, one to determine who would stand at the summit.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:16.080
Azuma Kazuma and Kawachi Kyousuke of

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:19.790
the Southern Tokyo branch, who were to participate in this,

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:22.460
had to be able to pass the preliminaries,
whose topic was to make dinner bread

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:24.680
on which it is hard for mold to grow.

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:33.760
This is the wasabi dinner bread, <i>Japan</i> #32.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:39.010
This is Kawachi style-sake-bread,
which will become <i>Osaka-pan</i> #1.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.360
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:45.270
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:47.530
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:50.970
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:56.200
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:59.840
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:17.050
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:25.020
In every place, there are people looking up at the sky.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:32.900
Under the night sky, we, who are whistling...

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:40.610
without words, are just tracing constellations with our fingers.

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:48.080
The dreams of the cold-sensitive... Your cold hands...

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:57.460
The warming magic is to believe in one path.

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:06.220
The single star found on the other side of the comet cloud...

00:02:06.470 --> 00:02:10.480
whether it be a shining or a faint star...

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:13.480
is the light of only you.

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:17.220
On the other side of the cloud in your heart,

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:22.030
is a sign post that remains unseen.

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:29.750
Now, opening these hands, what will you believe in today?

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:33.970
Each One’s Opening Curtain!!

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:36.140
The Pantasia Newcomers Battle Begins!

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:40.220
is three weeks...
Time until the newcomers battle finals

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.220
If I build up my muscles,

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:49.480
I’ll attain a power similar to that of Solar Hands,

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:51.950
the Solar Gauntlets.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:55.790
There’s no doubt that I’ll pass the preliminaries with my Osaka-pan #1.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:59.450
The problem is the newcomers
battle finals that lie ahead.

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:02.570
If only I were to attain the Solar Gauntlets,

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:05.450
I’d be able to win against Azuma and Suwabara.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.920
Then, the victor’s award of 1 million yen,

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:12.500
and the possibility of getting into Pantasia’s
main store, will fall into my hands.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:17.380
He’s moving forward and training
by himself, even while working...

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.380
I no longer see any hesitation in him.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:24.930
Kawachi-san.

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:27.890
Should we start increasing the weight that
you carry on your wrists by a little?

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:29.730
Sure...

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:33.400
If we don’t increase each weight to at least
5 kilos, I won’t be feeling it anymore.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.400
Wow! That’s really promising.

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:39.160
Kawachi, that’s really cool.

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:41.290
This is cool?

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:44.870
Fine, then I’ll give it to you.
I no longer need these weights.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:46.990
Yeah!

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:49.580
These are really heavy.

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:50.500
Azuma!

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:55.630
That’s some muscle there.

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:56.960
For winning against you.

00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:58.210
To win against me?

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:00.180
At arm wrestling?

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:01.390
Of course not!

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:02.430
Whatever.

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:05.220
If you think I’m the same as before,
you’re making a big mistake.

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:07.730
I’ll win!

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:09.850
I will not lose to you, even if I die.

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:11.400
Remember that well.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:12.020
Kawachi.

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:12.850
Oh, that’s right.
Kawachi.

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:12.860
Oh, that’s right.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:16.030
Don’t speak to me unnecessarily
for a while.

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:18.700
I don’t want to talk to you.

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:20.830
Kawachi...

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:25.410
Pantasia Main Store

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.580
Room temperature: 23°C.

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:30.290
Room humidity: 55%.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:33.010
The conditions of a regular room are being maintained.

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:45.840
Forward!

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:56.070
Of the 512 newcomers,

00:04:56.070 --> 00:04:58.900
just about half,

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:01.150
226 that is, submitted a bread that did not grow mold.

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:04.710
With so many submissions, despite
however much we’ve warned them,

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:07.000
there will be some that try to cheat.

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:15.000
Nawata Masaki, of the Sapporo branch.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.430
Hayashi Masato, of the Northern Ginma branch.

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:21.310
Nomura Atsushi, of the Kyuushuu Main branch.

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:24.680
Disqualified for the illegal use of artificial preservatives.

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:25.560
Trash.

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:28.770
What about them?

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:31.060
The two from Matsushiro’s place?

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:34.770
They still remain, at present.

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:37.810
Whether their bread will grow mold over the
next 3 weeks or not, we still don’t know.

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:39.810
It won’t grow.

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:43.150
I will never acknowledge the fact that artisans,

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:45.910
who cannot even pass the preliminaries,

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:46.820
could push me aside!

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:49.620
That’s right.

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:51.080
If they don’t come,

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:53.330
all meaning of my taking part in the finals will be lost.

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:58.250
I will definitely return the debt I owe from that time.

00:05:58.710 --> 00:05:59.800
Suwabara...

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:03.000
eagerness is a good thing, but...
if you lose, you won’t be let off lightly.

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:07.100
If a Main Store employee who was
exempt from the preliminaries

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:09.310
loses in the first round of the main stage...

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:13.010
you can safely assume that you
have no future in Pantasia.

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:15.520
Me? Lose in the first round?

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:17.070
Ridiculous!

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:42.210
There’s no hesitation in my swordsmanship.

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:46.680
Such a waste...

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:48.850
Kai,

00:06:48.850 --> 00:06:50.430
why do you wish to follow the
path of excelling at bread,

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:53.110
when you possess a skill as great as this?

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:55.220
Master.

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:58.730
The path of the sword is one in which life is destroyed.

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:02.730
However, the path of bread is one of life.

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:05.110
That is all.

00:07:06.770 --> 00:07:08.770
The path of the sword cannot save people,

00:07:08.770 --> 00:07:10.820
but the path of bread can help them live.

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:12.870
Is that what you’re saying?

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:15.780
However, Kai...

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:18.860
that expression on your face is not very convincing.

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:23.500
Because that is not the expression
of one wanting to help people live.

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:27.760
That’s none of your business.

00:07:34.170 --> 00:07:35.300
Kawachi...

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:38.220
I’ll win!

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:40.390
I will not lose to you, even if I die.

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:42.190
I don’t want to talk to you.

00:07:46.890 --> 00:07:47.860
Azuma...

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:51.700
Manager.

00:07:55.230 --> 00:07:57.580
I don’t know the reason, but...

00:07:58.190 --> 00:08:02.580
it seems that Kawachi hates me.

00:08:02.950 --> 00:08:04.960
That can’t be true, can it?

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:07.790
But Kawachi said that he’d win against me.

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:10.580
You try to win against someone
only if you hate them, right?

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:12.540
I like Kawachi,

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:14.890
so I don’t think that I want to win against him.

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:19.880
He hasn’t returned to our room in the boarding house for a long time, either.

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:22.760
He doesn’t even want to see my face.

00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:24.060
He hates me.

00:08:24.550 --> 00:08:25.930
Listen up, Azuma,

00:08:25.930 --> 00:08:29.940
you’ve been acknowledged by Kawachi... as a man.

00:08:32.020 --> 00:08:33.200
A man?

00:08:33.770 --> 00:08:35.160
That’s right. A man.

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:37.990
I’ve been a man ever since I was born.

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:41.040
I didn’t quite mean it that way.

00:08:41.990 --> 00:08:43.110
Listen up!

00:08:43.110 --> 00:08:46.410
Almost nobody’s enough of an idiot to go that far,

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:49.800
just to win against someone he hated.

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:52.960
Because you’re a person whom
he has acknowledged as a man,

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:57.850
Kawachi is seriously trying to win
against you, as an artisan.

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:02.560
What should... I do?

00:09:03.090 --> 00:09:06.640
When someone comes at you with all he has,
you face him with all you’ve got.

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:08.720
That is a man’s etiquette.

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:09.700
That is, a true rival.

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:12.690
A true rival.

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:19.910
It’s written as “Kan,” and read as “Otoko.”

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:22.650
It’s what a true man is.

00:09:22.650 --> 00:09:23.000
Azuma Kazuma.

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:24.070
Man
Azuma Kazuma.

00:09:24.070 --> 00:09:25.170
If you wish to stand as a man,
Man

00:09:25.170 --> 00:09:26.250
If you wish to stand as a man,

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:29.750
then use this afro!

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:43.590
Oh, Azuma-san,

00:09:43.590 --> 00:09:45.350
are you going out somewhere again?

00:09:47.430 --> 00:09:48.850
To Gifu.

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:49.860
To Gifu?

00:09:51.810 --> 00:09:55.150
Kawachi. You’re my rival.

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:57.230
So I’ll definitely win, too.

00:09:57.230 --> 00:09:59.110
For that, I’m going to Gifu.

00:10:04.780 --> 00:10:06.290
Bring it on.

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:25.630
It’s finally over.

00:10:25.630 --> 00:10:27.730
It’s more intensive training again at the gym from here.

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:28.730
Huh?

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:33.770
What in the world... is this?

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:44.440
Afro
(For Kawachi’s use)

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:45.150
Why?
Afro
(For Kawachi’s use)

00:10:45.150 --> 00:10:45.620
Afro
(For Kawachi’s use)

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:46.880
is one week...
Time until the newcomers battle finals

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:49.500
Thank goodness, there isn’t one for me.

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:50.540
is one week...
Time until the newcomers battle finals

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:56.680
Gifu: The outskirts of Toki city

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:15.770
The clay from around here looks really good, too.

00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:28.160
Something like this is no big deal.

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:32.210
Grandpa Umasaburou!

00:11:34.910 --> 00:11:37.420
I got quite a bit today.

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:40.170
Oh, you’ve worked hard.

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:43.680
With this much, we should be able to make “that.”

00:11:45.670 --> 00:11:47.510
This earth around the outskirts of Toki city

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:51.970
has a high content of the special ingredient petalite.

00:11:51.970 --> 00:11:55.100
It’s indispensable for making “that.”

00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:57.390
First of all, petalite is...

00:11:57.390 --> 00:11:59.600
I’m tired of hearing about that
bit of your vast knowledge.

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:01.060
Please make it quickly.

00:12:01.060 --> 00:12:02.480
Leave it to me!

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:06.690
This Azuma Umasaburou, who
was called Japan’s #1 artisan,

00:12:06.690 --> 00:12:09.790
will still not lose to anyone who is younger!

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:13.490
Let’s make Japan’s #1 fired product!

00:12:13.490 --> 00:12:16.000
I’m depending on you,
Grandpa Umasaburou.

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:21.080
But Umatarou has a good grandson, doesn’t he?

00:12:21.080 --> 00:12:24.130
He’s probably really happy beneath the
shadows of the leaves and the flowers.

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:25.750
He’s not dead yet!

00:12:25.750 --> 00:12:28.090
My grandfather’s still alive.

00:12:28.090 --> 00:12:28.810
What?

00:12:30.380 --> 00:12:32.850
Grandpa Umatarou is still as lively as ever.

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:34.600
Is that so?

00:12:34.600 --> 00:12:35.810
In that case...

00:12:43.270 --> 00:12:44.820
This will do.

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:50.240
You shouldn’t make your mortuary tablet yourself!

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:53.620
Aren’t you also still living?

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:54.990
It doesn’t matter.

00:12:54.990 --> 00:12:56.990
Sooner or later, people die.

00:12:56.990 --> 00:13:00.550
If I don’t have such a level of preparedness,
I cannot make “that.”

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:03.750
Kazuma, let’s get to it immediately!

00:13:03.750 --> 00:13:04.510
O-Okay.

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:13.730
Note: A silly rhyme. Sakana = “fish.”
Yaketa ka na = “wonder if it’s grilled.”
I wonder if the fish have been grilled yet.

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:14.760
is three days...
Time until the newcomers battle finals

00:13:14.760 --> 00:13:17.030
The results of the preliminaries have come in...

00:13:17.030 --> 00:13:18.560
So, what are the results?

00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:27.080
Report of results

00:13:34.450 --> 00:13:37.240
D-Don’t tell me... Did we both fail?

00:13:37.240 --> 00:13:39.210
Or is that just one of us...

00:13:40.450 --> 00:13:42.290
You’ve passed the preliminaries.

00:13:42.290 --> 00:13:43.340
Both of you.

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:45.460
Hang on!

00:13:45.460 --> 00:13:46.840
Don’t do such confusing things!

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:48.260
Manager!

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:53.340
It was today’s lunch, wasn’t it?

00:13:53.340 --> 00:13:55.050
Thanks for the treat.

00:13:55.050 --> 00:13:57.020
Hang on, just once more!

00:13:57.640 --> 00:13:58.970
That’s not right.

00:13:58.970 --> 00:14:02.140
I made sure to bet on both of you passing.

00:14:02.140 --> 00:14:04.980
Also, this was something that the manager suggested.

00:14:04.980 --> 00:14:05.490
That’s not the problem.
Also, this was something that the manager suggested.

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:06.560
That’s not the problem.

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:09.870
And by the way, what I bet on is a secret.

00:14:10.360 --> 00:14:11.580
Moreover...

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:13.080
Kawachi.

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:19.670
Manager...

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:30.690
It’s still not quite up to mark, is it?

00:14:30.690 --> 00:14:31.340
Huh?

00:14:31.340 --> 00:14:33.010
Hands. Your hands.

00:14:33.670 --> 00:14:34.510
I guess...

00:14:34.510 --> 00:14:36.980
Well, I guess it’s good enough for one month’s work.

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:40.360
However, there’s still more work required
for obtaining the Solar Gauntlets.

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:41.610
Yes!

00:14:42.930 --> 00:14:45.770
Everyone, your big brother’s going to do it.

00:14:45.770 --> 00:14:47.900
He’s definitely going to win.

00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:55.910
It’s almost complete.

00:14:57.240 --> 00:14:59.080
By the way, Kazuma,

00:14:59.530 --> 00:15:03.090
when this is done, will you bake one for me first?

00:15:03.090 --> 00:15:06.600
I want to eat it once more before I die.

00:15:07.250 --> 00:15:10.290
The best of the <i>Japan</i> masterpieces,

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:12.340
<i>Japan</i> #44!

00:15:12.880 --> 00:15:14.760
Of course.

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:19.060
I’ll make one more delicious than
ever, Grandpa Umasaburou!

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:22.980
I’m so happy...

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:29.660
I see it. I’ll win!

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:30.190
is one day...
Time until the newcomers battle finals

00:15:30.190 --> 00:15:33.360
I wonder if Azuma-san is all right...

00:15:33.360 --> 00:15:37.670
It’s been 3 weeks since the news reached us.
Even I’m beginning to get worried...

00:15:38.280 --> 00:15:41.370
He messed around in Izu and Miura quite a bit, too...

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:44.580
I hope he didn’t try to run to Gifu.

00:15:45.830 --> 00:15:48.960
It could be that he’s completely
forgotten about the finals,

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:51.080
and is taking it easy in Gifu.

00:15:51.080 --> 00:15:52.840
That’s possible, isn’t it?

00:15:54.090 --> 00:15:57.170
I’ll try calling Azuma-san’s home.

00:15:57.170 --> 00:15:59.560
We may be able to figure out
what the circumstances are.

00:16:01.550 --> 00:16:02.600
Gifu?

00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:07.110
In that case, he’s probably at
his Grandpa Umasaburou’s.

00:16:07.110 --> 00:16:09.690
Oh, is that so?

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:11.520
Then, please do.

00:16:11.520 --> 00:16:13.280
Okay, I’m hanging up then.

00:16:14.520 --> 00:16:17.480
It appears that he has some relatives in Gifu.

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:19.360
So, he’s probably over there.

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:21.620
We should be able to get in touch with him.

00:16:22.030 --> 00:16:23.530
That idiot.

00:16:23.530 --> 00:16:25.580
The first day of the finals is tomorrow.

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:27.250
Does he really understand?

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:31.540
Hmm? Grandpa!

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:34.250
Where’s Grandpa Umasaburou’s phone number?

00:16:34.250 --> 00:16:36.670
We don’t have such a thing.

00:16:36.670 --> 00:16:38.840
He doesn’t have a phone.

00:16:38.840 --> 00:16:41.270
Because he’s not a Momo like me.

00:16:41.270 --> 00:16:42.770
Nomo?

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:47.020
The one in the Major Leagues?

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:47.930
Tornado
The one in the Major Leagues?

00:16:47.930 --> 00:16:49.270
No!
Tornado

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:49.280
No!

00:16:49.280 --> 00:16:52.350
Momo of Modern Boy!

00:16:52.350 --> 00:16:55.910
It’s like the story of the boy Kindaichi.

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:59.360
What part of Grandpa is Modern Boy?

00:16:59.360 --> 00:17:00.780
This part...

00:17:00.780 --> 00:17:05.280
This part is Momo, the same as that
of Kazuma, who’s gone to Tokyo.

00:17:05.280 --> 00:17:11.410
I’m the smartest in the world...

00:17:11.410 --> 00:17:12.830
Well, it can’t be helped.

00:17:12.830 --> 00:17:14.300
I guess I’ll have to go...

00:17:34.190 --> 00:17:35.860
I overslept!

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:38.160
I have to go! This is terrible!

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:47.290
Kazuma!

00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:50.250
Sis!

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:52.300
You really cause a lot of trouble, don’t you?

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:55.050
I’ll give you a ride to Tokyo.

00:17:56.580 --> 00:17:57.630
Grandpa.

00:17:57.630 --> 00:17:58.800
Grandpa Umasaburou.

00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:00.800
Grandpa Umasaburou.

00:18:01.920 --> 00:18:02.810
Is something wrong?

00:18:03.340 --> 00:18:05.310
He’s so soundly asleep that he won’t wake up.

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:07.850
Poor thing, don’t wake him up.

00:18:07.850 --> 00:18:09.640
Where are you going?

00:18:09.640 --> 00:18:11.360
The toilet, the toilet.

00:18:12.230 --> 00:18:13.730
Okay, this is it.

00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:17.940
Thank you for this, Grandpa Umasaburou.

00:18:17.940 --> 00:18:20.450
I’ll make #44 again.

00:18:21.110 --> 00:18:21.870
See ya.

00:18:23.150 --> 00:18:25.780
Kazuma, thank you.

00:18:25.780 --> 00:18:28.200
Being able to live with you in the end,

00:18:28.200 --> 00:18:30.870
and being able to do the best job ever,

00:18:30.870 --> 00:18:33.260
I was really happy.

00:18:33.260 --> 00:18:37.010
But the scary <i>Japan</i> #44...

00:18:37.010 --> 00:18:41.010
it was so good that I transcended
into the next phase of death.

00:18:41.010 --> 00:18:43.050
Azuma Umasaburou

00:18:43.050 --> 00:18:45.430
That was supposed to be a joke, you know...

00:18:51.680 --> 00:18:54.320
He’s forgetting it.
The proof of being Momo.

00:18:58.230 --> 00:18:59.440
Yeah, Yeah, Yeah!

00:18:59.440 --> 00:19:01.360
Hang on tight!

00:19:02.190 --> 00:19:03.820
I’m going to die.

00:19:03.820 --> 00:19:05.580
Sis! I don’t want to die!

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:07.240
Sis!

00:19:07.240 --> 00:19:09.870
I beg you! A little slower!

00:19:16.370 --> 00:19:18.630
That idiot!

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:20.180
He’s not here!

00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:24.140
He may have really forgotten about the finals.

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:26.140
What do we do, Manager?

00:19:26.140 --> 00:19:27.770
I don’t know!

00:19:28.430 --> 00:19:30.180
Man...

00:19:30.180 --> 00:19:33.680
just when I’ve obtained the Solar Gauntlets...

00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:35.520
This is dodging the problem...

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:36.530
Kawachi.

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:40.360
Suwabara... Kai.

00:19:42.900 --> 00:19:45.030
Where’s the other youngster?

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:48.610
The two of you together
have hurt my pride.

00:19:48.610 --> 00:19:50.250
There’s one more coward.

00:19:51.780 --> 00:19:54.250
Being alone, you might find it
too much to handle, right?

00:19:56.080 --> 00:20:00.260
Either way, the two of you must need
to team up to pass the finals, right?

00:20:00.790 --> 00:20:02.960
Azuma is my rival.

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:05.260
So, I will beat Azuma.

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:08.020
And Suwabara!

00:20:08.840 --> 00:20:12.270
I plan to fight you fair and square, and then win.

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:13.850
Oh?

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:15.860
That’s a good expression you have there.

00:20:17.480 --> 00:20:21.150
Let’s see you come up to my feet.

00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:21.780
That’s an order.

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:23.820
Suwabara...

00:20:26.030 --> 00:20:28.570
Azuma, what are you doing?

00:20:28.570 --> 00:20:30.450
Hurry up!

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:37.200
This is no good.

00:20:37.200 --> 00:20:40.710
At this rate, I won’t make it.

00:20:41.120 --> 00:20:42.340
I’ll run.

00:20:42.340 --> 00:20:44.720
Kazuma. You forgot this.

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:50.510
Good luck!

00:20:50.510 --> 00:20:51.310
Yeah!

00:20:52.010 --> 00:20:54.780
If you lose, I’ll beat you up.

00:20:55.310 --> 00:20:56.360
O-Okay.

00:20:59.980 --> 00:21:01.530
Attention please.

00:21:02.350 --> 00:21:06.870
We’ll now begin the Pantasia newcomers battle finals.

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:09.030
and Bicycles
Pedestrian

00:21:12.610 --> 00:21:17.290
I... am your examiner, Kuroyanagi Ryou.

00:21:18.080 --> 00:21:21.040
The winner will receive a monetary
award of 1 million yen,

00:21:21.040 --> 00:21:24.170
and an extra prize of three months
of studying abroad in France.

00:21:24.170 --> 00:21:28.010
Also, the winner can look forward to
an appointment at the Main Store.

00:21:31.130 --> 00:21:33.720
“Okay, let’s explain the method of the competition,” is

00:21:33.720 --> 00:21:35.890
what I’d like to say, but...

00:21:35.890 --> 00:21:40.230
This time, of the 510 newcomers, 58,

00:21:40.230 --> 00:21:43.360
which is more than expected, passed.

00:21:43.810 --> 00:21:44.940
So...

00:21:46.730 --> 00:21:49.150
He just doesn’t mature...

00:21:49.150 --> 00:21:50.580
It looks like I made it in time.

00:21:59.740 --> 00:22:00.880
Azuma.

00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:03.620
Azuma-san.

00:22:03.620 --> 00:22:05.300
We were worried.

00:22:06.130 --> 00:22:07.300
What is it?

00:22:08.130 --> 00:22:10.130
I made it in time, so it’s okay, right?

00:22:10.130 --> 00:22:12.010
You’re late again?

00:22:12.010 --> 00:22:12.380
You...

00:22:12.380 --> 00:22:15.510
Oh, you’re going to be the examiner again?

00:22:15.510 --> 00:22:17.690
Old man Kuroyanagi!

00:22:18.180 --> 00:22:19.930
Old man?

00:22:19.930 --> 00:22:23.140
I, who is only 22 years old, is being called...

00:22:23.140 --> 00:22:24.560
Azuma Kazuma!

00:22:24.560 --> 00:22:27.150
For being 5 minutes late, minus 5 points!

00:22:27.150 --> 00:22:28.910
What?!

00:22:31.280 --> 00:22:33.950
It’s a scene that I’ve seen somewhere before.

00:22:38.500 --> 00:22:46.640
If I think of you, and even utter the clichéd phrase “I love you,”

00:22:47.210 --> 00:22:55.650
it makes such a nice sound, and you continue talking.

00:22:59.220 --> 00:23:06.660
The hopeless tears your bold self sometimes shows me form flag of truce.

00:23:07.960 --> 00:23:11.830
If nothing is said, then all the more,

00:23:12.030 --> 00:23:17.970
I just can’t look away. Things like sadness and pain...

00:23:17.970 --> 00:23:20.540
Well, that happens a lot in life, after all.

00:23:20.770 --> 00:23:24.680
When you casually say, “Do your best,” it gives me strength.

00:23:25.120 --> 00:23:29.450
Whenever your small back trembles, I will embrace you right away.

00:23:30.480 --> 00:23:33.290
Even if the scenery outside my window changes...

00:23:33.780 --> 00:23:37.990
Stay with me as you are, bad sleeping habits and all.

00:23:38.620 --> 00:23:43.160
If you sulk, and utter

00:23:43.430 --> 00:23:51.970
Even the clichéd “I hate you,” it comes across as the opposite.

00:23:52.370 --> 00:24:01.330
I will love you, no matter what. It’s just another Sunday to me.

00:24:06.040 --> 00:24:07.840
The next task is butter rolls!

00:24:07.840 --> 00:24:09.340
First, choose your butter!

00:24:09.340 --> 00:24:10.340
Okay, I’ll go with this one.

00:24:10.340 --> 00:24:12.190
Don’t! Don’t do it, Azuma!

00:24:12.190 --> 00:24:14.230
That’s... That one is...!!

00:24:14.230 --> 00:24:15.970
Next time, Yakitate Japan:

00:24:15.970 --> 00:24:18.520
Garbage and trash!!
Kazuma selected the worst possible butter!

00:24:18.520 --> 00:24:19.980
Be sure to watch!

00:24:20.390 --> 00:24:22.730
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:23.220 --> 00:24:25.770
The name of the place Gifu was
given by Oda Nobunaga.

00:24:25.770 --> 00:24:27.770
The “Gi” comes from “Gisan,” and
the “Fu” comes from “Kyokufu.”

00:24:27.770 --> 00:24:31.740
It’s the only administrative division
of Japan with a Chinese name.

00:24:32.980 --> 00:24:34.910
But that has nothing to do with us, does it?
